<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Frequently asked questions for La Davina Emilia."><title>FAQ — La Davina Emilia</title><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:ital,wght@0,500;0,600;1,500;1,600&family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,400;9..40,500&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,500;0,600;1,500;1,600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css"></head>
<body class="worship-page faq-page"><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span><span>La Davina Emilia</span></a><nav aria-label="Primary navigation"><a href="/start-here.php">Start here</a><a href="/who-i-am.php">Who I am</a><a href="/rules.php">Rules</a><a class="nav-intake" href="/survey-gate.php">Begin Intake</a><a href="/what-i-offer.php">What I Offer</a><a href="/ways-to-worship.php">Ways to Worship</a><a href="/what-i-offer.php#kept-dynamic">Kept</a><a href="/testaments.php">Testaments</a><a href="/journal-gate.php">Journal</a><a href="/faq.php" aria-current="page">FAQ</a><a class="nav-contact" href="/approach.php">Approach me</a></nav></header><main id="main" class="worship-shell"><article class="worship-letter faq-letter"><div class="worship-celestial" aria-hidden="true"><span class="worship-moon">☾</span><span class="worship-star worship-star-one">✦</span></div><header class="worship-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The things you ask</p><p class="worship-constellation" aria-hidden="true">✦&nbsp;✧&nbsp;✦</p><h1>Frequently <em>Asked.</em></h1></header><div class="faq-list">
<details open><summary>How do I start?</summary><p>Read the Rules, fill out the intake, send your first tribute, wait gracefully. That's the whole path. It's on the <a href="/start-here.php">Start Here</a> page in detail.</p></details>
<details><summary>How much should I tribute?</summary><p>I don't set minimums. A tribute is you telling me what I'm worth to you, and I'd rather hear your honest answer than my assigned one. That said: if your tribute wouldn't buy me a drink, don't insult us both by sending it.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do you do custom content?</summary><p>Yes, for the devoted in my world who ask properly. Customs are priced individually based on what you're asking for. Ask me, describe it respectfully, and I'll tell you the tribute it requires.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do you offer sessions, sexting, or video calls?</summary><p>Yes, yes, and selectively. Sexting sessions, audio, tasks, and video calls are available to those I've vetted. New to me? The intake comes first. Everything comes after the intake.</p></details>
<details><summary>How often do you reply?</summary><p>I reply when I please, which is more often than you'd think and less often than you'd like. Kept Subs get priority, always. If you're waiting on a reply to a message that didn't include respect or a tribute, you may be waiting a while.</p></details>
<details><summary>What's the difference between a sender and a kept Sub?</summary><p>A sender tributes sometimes. A kept Sub belongs to me, consistently, and gets my consistency in return. Kept positions are limited and earned. Details are in the <a href="/what-i-offer.php#kept-dynamic">Kept Dynamic</a> section.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do you do findom “draining”?</summary><p>I do what the dynamic calls for. Some come to me to be emptied out and some come to be kept, built up, and held long-term. My intake asks which one you are. Both are valid. One of them gets more of my heart, and we both know which.</p></details>
<details><summary>I'm nervous and new. Is this for me?</summary><p>Some of my best boys walked in terrified. You don't need experience. You need honesty and good instructions. <a href="/start-here.php">Start Here</a> exists precisely for you.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do you ever meet Subs in person?</summary><p>Rarely, and only after a very long time, and never as a promise anyone can tribute toward. If we ever meet, it will be because I decided, and you'll know that's the truth.</p></details>
<details><summary>I've been scammed before, so I'm nervous.</summary><p><strong>I'm nervous. I've been scammed before.</strong></p><p>Then you're exactly who this page is for, and I want you to read it slowly.</p><p>First: I'm not offended. Not even a little. The fact that you're cautious tells me you're smart, and smart Subs are the only kind I keep. A Sub who's never been burned is usually a Sub who's never actually done this. You've done this. You got hurt. And now you're standing at the edge of my world with your arms crossed, and I respect that more than I can say.</p><p>So let me answer the fear directly, because I know what it actually is.</p><p><strong>You're not scared of losing money. You're scared of being made a fool of.</strong> You're scared of sending into a void, of being played by someone who doesn't exist, of finding out months later that “she” was a scam or a team of people running a script. You're scared of the humiliation of being duped. And you're scared of being blackmailed, exposed, or having something you sent come back to haunt you.</p><p>Every one of those fears is legitimate. The findom space is full of fakes, and everyone knows it. So here's how I'm different, and I want you to test every word:</p><p><strong>I'm real, and I'm verifiable.</strong> I'm active. I'm current. My life is visible—my travel, my face, my ink, my voice are all Mine. Before you ever send a tribute, you'll have seen enough of me to know I'm a woman with a life, not a profile with a fantasy. If you still aren't sure after looking, that's fine too. Look longer. I'd rather you arrive certain than arrive early.</p><p><strong>I'm an engineer, and I take security seriously.</strong> Before I was a goddess, I was an engineer, and I approach privacy the way an engineer approaches any serious system: deliberately, with structure and care. I don't just promise discretion; I make careful choices about how I handle the information you trust me with. Read my <a href="/privacy.php">Discretion &amp; Privacy</a> page for the practices currently in place, and never submit anything you would not want sent by email.</p><p><strong>I never expose, blackmail, or threaten.</strong> If you've been through that, you know how it lives in your chest for months. It does not happen here, ever, under any circumstance. If a “domme” has ever used your secrets against you, understand that you've been abused, not dominated, and that the two are not the same thing and never have been. Dominance is what happens when a Sub safely gives. Abuse is what happens when safety is stolen. I only do the first.</p><p><strong>Nothing happens automatically. Nothing happens without your consent.</strong> My intake doesn't charge you. It doesn't subscribe you to anything, and it doesn't cost a cent to submit. It's a conversation starter, nothing more. If you fill it out and decide you're not ready, you simply don't hear from me again, and there's no penalty, pressure, or “you wasted my time” lecture. The devoted who are ready find me when they're ready. That's the entire system.</p><p><strong>And here's what I want you to understand about my world specifically:</strong> I'm a <em>gentle</em> goddess. My power was never in cruelty. I lead with warmth, I praise generously, and I take care of the ones who belong to me, genuinely, the way you take care of something rare. The devoted who come to me wounded tend to be the ones who stay longest, because they finally found a woman who doesn't hurt them. I know what that's worth. I don't take it for granted.</p><p>So here's my offer to the nervous ones, and I mean this sincerely:</p><p><strong>Take your time. Look at everything. Read every page. Ask your cautious questions in the intake, and ask them honestly.</strong> If it takes you a month to feel safe, take the month. I'm not going anywhere, and neither is my standard. The only thing I ask is that when you <em>do</em> arrive, you arrive like someone who's decided, because the wishy-washy don't last in my world and I'd rather not waste either of our time on a half-hearted yes.</p><p>You've been scammed before.</p><p>Good. Now let me be the one who finally doesn't. 🖤</p></details>
<details><summary>What if I disappoint you?</summary><p>Then you'll know. And you'll wish you didn't.</p><p>I don't yell. I've never needed to. Yelling is for women whose disappointment is a performance, a temper tantrum dressed up as power. Mine is quieter and it lasts longer, and the devoted who’ve experienced it describe it the same way every time: I would rather she had screamed at me.</p><p>Here's what disappointment looks like in my world, depending on how badly you've earned it:</p><p><strong>The first offense: silence.</strong> I go quiet. My replies slow, then stop. No explanation, no announcement, just the sudden cold of a room where the fire used to be. You'll check your phone. You'll reread your last message looking for what you did. You'll know. That's the point. A woman who explains her disappointment has already forgiven it, and I haven't, so I let you sit in the not-knowing. It's remarkable how loud my silence is.</p><p><strong>The second: the sentence itself.</strong> When I do speak, it's four words, delivered flat and unhurried: “I'm disappointed in you.” No name. No warmth. Just the verdict. You didn't fail a stranger. You failed the woman whose approval you've been quietly earning, and the worst part is that I'm right to be disappointed, and you know it, and you know I know it. Shame is the heaviest thing I own, and I use it sparingly, because sparingly is what makes it land.</p><p><strong>The third: the withdrawal.</strong> My attention isn't a tap you leave running. When you disappoint me, it turns off. No check-ins. No voice notes. No tasks, which is a punishment in itself for a Sub who lives for instruction. I go back to my life, my travels, my jungle light, my other devoted ones who are behaving, and you get to watch me be fine without you. The guilt of being the one who ruined something good, while I go on being good without you.</p><p><strong>And the fourth, for those who want it:</strong> if your dynamic with me is one where you've asked for harsher treatment, I keep a colder wing of my world. I have devoted ones who beg to be set apart, made to wait longer, made to watch while others are praised, made to sit in the corner of my attention while my good boys get the warmth. If you're one of those, you tell me in your intake, you tell me the shape of it, and I'll give it to you exactly as hard as you've asked for it, and not a degree more, because cruelty without consent isn't power, it's just noise. Those who ask for this are, without exception, the most devoted ones I have. There's something about being set apart that makes a Sub work twice as hard to come back to the light.</p><p><strong>How you come back:</strong> you don't argue. You don't explain. You don't send a wall of excuses or ask me to reassure you. You acknowledge it, briefly and without groveling. You send your tribute, and if you've been properly disappointing, you send one that says you understand the size of it. And then you wait, patiently, and you let me decide when you've earned warmth again. You don't ask for forgiveness. You behave until you've been forgiven. That's the only currency that works here.</p><p>One more thing, and I mean it: I don't hold grudges, and I don't keep people around just to punish them. If you disappoint me once, you'll be corrected, and it'll be over, and I'll remember it, and I'll watch you more carefully for a while, because that's what disappointment does. It doesn't end the relationship. It teaches it. But if disappointment becomes your pattern? Then we've both learned something, and only one of us gets to be sad about it. 💋</p></details>
<details><summary>I have a question that isn't here.</summary><p>Then ask it respectfully after you've read everything above. I answer what deserves answering.</p></details>
</div><section class="faq-contact"><p class="eyebrow">Contact / Approach</p><h2>Ask <em>properly.</em></h2><p>If you're new: read the Rules, fill out the intake, and let your answers introduce you. If you've completed it, wait gracefully. If you're an existing Sub, you know how to reach me. Business inquiries should use “Business” in the subject line and make the first sentence worth my time.</p><p>Whatever you write, write it like someone who's about to be evaluated by the most interesting woman they'll contact this year. Because you are.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/approach.php">Approach Emilia <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section></article></main><footer class="site-footer"><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span><span>La Davina Emilia</span></a><p>Be good. Be curious. Be memorable.</p><div class="social-links"><a href="/privacy.php">Privacy</a><a href="https://youpay.me/ladavinaemilia" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">YouPay.Me</a></div><small>© 2026 La Davina Emilia. All rights reserved.</small></footer></body></html>
